   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["ReduceSpinorProducts", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Reduces spinor chains and traces using ordinary identities and \
external on-shell conditions.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"ReduceSpinorProducts", "[", "expr",
         "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "returns a reduced expression using \
bounded, directed algebraic passes."}], "Usage"],
  Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["The reducer handles chain reversal, \
momentum-slot linearity, supported Clifford contractions, external Dirac \
equations, Schouten contractions and exact polynomial/rational \
simplifications.", "Notes"], Cell["It does not infer total momentum \
conservation and does not impose diagram-local internal on-shell conditions. \
PrepareAmplitudes supplies process information for those additional \
operations.", "Notes"], Cell["Momentum sums and Multiparticle insertions can \
be expanded where useful. Shared scalar factors and opaque physical PropDen \
factors are retained where possible.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Automatic rules have a directed simplification order and finite \
expansion limits. The result is not a proof of a globally minimal form. For \
an explicit derivation, retain each SpinorIdentityCandidates edit and its \
assumptions.", "Notes"], Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
the local HEPCAT checkout; no model parameters are assigned global numerical \
values.", "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"If", "[", "!", "StringQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", " ", "||", " ", "!", "DirectoryQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ",
         "Global`$HEPCATpath", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "First", "[", "PacletFind", "[", "\"HEPCAT\"", "]", "]", "[",
         "\"Location\"", "]", ",", " ", "\"source\"", "}", "]", "]", ";",
         "\n", "If", "[", "!", "MemberQ", "[", "$Packages", ",", " ",
